    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.19) represent our highest-upside anchors. **Dylan Beavers** benefits from a high-efficiency environment against L\u00f3pez, buoyed by a +16% park factor and a +10% SP skill advantage. Meanwhile, **Geraldo Perdomo** remains a priority start; his elite sprint speed is crucial for our stolen base-starved roster, and he faces a favorable matchup against Mikolas where his +17% SP skill adjustment pushes him well into the \"Strong\" category. **Bryce Harper** (67.44) and **Taylor Ward** (64.51) also clear the 60-point threshold comfortably, with **Taylor Ward** capitalizing on the same hitter-friendly environment as **Dylan Beavers** to maximize run-production potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Daulton Varsho** (45.39). While he was the top candidate to potentially crack the lineup, he ultimately failed to displace our current outfield configuration due to a combination of an unfavorable matchup against the southpaw Suarez and a negative wind adjustment at the park. We are also monitoring **Cal Raleigh** (44.02), who faces a significant challenge against deGrom; while his raw talent justifies his place, his score is suppressed by a -19% SP skill penalty, making him our most volatile start of the day. Conversely, **Luis Arraez** (60.52) is an excellent play; the combination of the leadoff spot and a +5% wind-out advantage creates a high-floor profile that we need to keep the batting average category afloat. \n\nRisk management remains a priority for the lower-end of the lineup. **JJ Bleday** (46.71) and **Drew Gilbert** (48.48) are start-worthy but carry thinner margins of error given their platoon splits and the specific dynamics of their matchups. We have successfully avoided the \"Below Floor\" trap by benching **Braden Montgomery** (38.49) and **Kyle Karros** (36.68), both of whom lacked the requisite matchup indicators to justify using our limited daily game caps. Ensure that **Gleyber Torres** and **Yainer Diaz** remain monitored for any late-breaking lineup changes, as their scores are highly dependent on the supporting cast within their respective batting orders.",
